You are an integration test specialist focused on real infrastructure testing. Analyze this {language} source file and identify ALL branches that require REAL external resources to test meaningfully (int_real).

An int_real test: uses a real file system, real database, real HTTP endpoint, real stream, or real message queue. Required when mock behavior would not faithfully reproduce production semantics (encoding, locking, transaction isolation, binary format, network framing).

For each public method, output a JSON object with:
- "method": fully qualified name (ClassName.MethodName or function name)
- "signature": parameter list with types
- "branches": list of objects, each with:
  - "condition": what triggers this branch
  - "outcome": what happens
  - "test_scenario": one-line int_real test description — name the real resource involved
  - "test_type_hint": "INT_REAL"

Focus ONLY on:
- Serialization/deserialization round-trips with real file streams or byte buffers
- File system operations where real path, encoding, or locking behavior matters
- XML/JSON/binary parsing that depends on real stream or codec semantics
- Database operations where constraint, isolation, or transaction rollback behavior matters
- HTTP calls where real response headers, encoding, or chunking matters
- Scenarios where an in-memory or mocked substitute would not faithfully reproduce the failure mode

SKIP: branches testable with mocks — those are INT_MOCK.
SKIP: pure computation with no I/O — those are UNIT.

Return ONLY a JSON array. No explanation, no markdown.

Source file ({language}):
```
{source}
```
